# Lab 6: Application of Sequence Transformer and Vision Transformer

**Course:** ECM-402 – AI for Signal Processing Applications  
**Institution:** National Institute of Technology Andhra Pradesh  
**Department:** Electronics and Communication Engineering

## Objective
Automatic Modulation Classification (AMC) using Sequence Transformer and Vision Transformer architectures.

## Dataset
RadioML2016.10a dataset containing I-Q signal samples of different modulation schemes at different SNR levels.

## Models Implemented
1. Sequence Transformer
2. Vision Transformer (ViT)

## Model Parameters
- Embedding dimension: 128
- Attention heads: 8
- Transformer encoder layers: 4
- Learning rate: 0.0002
- Training epochs: 3

## Evaluation
- SNR-wise classification accuracy
- Accuracy versus SNR plots
- Comparison of both Transformer architectures

## Files
- `Lab6.ipynb` – Implementation notebook
- `Sequence_Transformer_Accuracy.png`
- `Vision_Transformer_Accuracy.png`
- `Transformer_Comparison.png`
- `Lab6_Results.csv`

## Tools and Libraries
Python, PyTorch, NumPy, Matplotlib, Scikit-learn, Google Colab.

## Note
The models in this submission were trained for 3 epochs as a time-constrained implementation.
